From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 20:24:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: <select> dropdowns

Bridge Servo's show_embedder_control(EmbedderControl::SelectElement) to
ACE's OnSelectPopupMenu. Unlike JS dialogs, ACE renders the dropdown menu
itself (via its overlay manager) and drives the callback, so no app
handler is needed: the shim hands ACE the flattened option labels + the
select's on-screen rect (concrete NWebSelectPopupMenuParam / MenuItem /
MenuBound), and ACE returns the picked option indices through an
NWebSelectPopupMenuCallback -> select_popup_continue/cancel -> an Action.
The (!Send) SelectElement is parked on the servo thread keyed by an id;
on a pick we select(indices) + submit(), on cancel we drop it (Drop
resubmits the unchanged selection). Option indices are the flat DOM order,
matching servo's option ids.

test_select.py opens the ACE menu, finds the option row via uitest
dumpLayout, taps it, and asserts the page's onchange fired (body colour).

Add wait_for_pixel / wait_until_stable to conftest and use them wherever a test
asserts on the result of a discrete interaction -- the select pick, but equally
the dialog resolve and link/back navigation, which had a fixed sleep-then-
capture. Polling for the expected frame removes the race with its present: a
lone capture is the premature-capture artifact that earlier read as blank frames
/ render latency.

hdc_py.cmd forwards to subprocess.run, which has no default timeout, so a servo
bug that wedges the ArkUI thread (blocking `uitest dumpLayout`) could hang a test
inside a command, never reaching the poll helpers' wall-clock deadlines. Pass a
30s timeout through sh() so such a hang surfaces as a TimeoutExpired failure
instead of stalling the run.

Verified on rk3568: tapping a <select> opens the ACE dropdown and picking
an option fires the page's change event with the chosen value (no crash;
the servo-thread OnSelectPopupMenu call, which ACE does not marshal, is
tolerated). Item font size/height are set so the labels render.

Validation: Test by running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_select.py on a device, then the full suite (uv run --with pytest --with hdc-py --with pillow python -m pytest ports/arkweb/tools); it must pass without hangs.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
